{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense","id":1022729,"title":"messianic voices intolerance makes no sense.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-27T07:02:31-08:00","id":1022729,"title":"messianic voices intolerance makes no sense.","content":"at least in my opinion.<br /> from dark ages mage core rule book: these guys believe in universal reconciliation<br /> in lay terms this means that(eventually) everyone gets saved.<br /> <br /> but here is the issue. historically the justification for christian intolerance(and torture and executions etc) were the following two things.<br /> 1)jesus said&quot;love god and love others as yourself&quot;<br /> 2)jesus said &quot;i am the way and the truth no one comes to the father etc&quot; or &quot;whoever denies me i will also deny before the father&quot; or &quot;but he who does not believe is already lost for he has denied the son&quot;<br /> <br /> these are generally interpreted to mean that non christians(and heretics or at least serious ones) go to hell. even if said hell is a limbo/paradise of the unsaved&quot;<br /> so if we accept the above premises it makes perfect sense. to try and destroy other religions by any and all means. because you genuinely wish to save these people. even if a &quot;few&quot; have to be &quot;lost&quot; to make an example to the rest.<br /> even in versions of christianity(such as eastern orthodoxy i believe) where non christians can be saved this logic can still be applied to an extend. after all the new testament's morality is still the best way to avoid hell.<br /> <br /> but if premise number 2) is entirely wrong...then what is the point of all that violence?<br /> <br /> unless you are a gabrielite who believes premise number 2) is correct","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T07:51:49-08:00","id":1022755,"title":"","content":"Realize that in WOD, just like in the real world, that not everything done in the name of God was done in the name of God. Many times is was (and sadly still is) simply their justification for their actions, no mater how wrong that justification is. Unfortunately, especially in the Middle Ages, acts of violence was often seen as the way to counter heretics, as was using God as an excuse to go to war. Aside from Israel's taking of the Promised Land there are not many times that God commanded them to go to war against other nations. Mostly (not all) their wars were in the defense of themselves, and often as a result of judgement upon Israel for their unfaithfulness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":987,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","user":"Tuch","date":". 12-27-2016, 10:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:16:17-08:00","id":1022792,"title":"","content":"Yup. They believe in&quot;universal reconciliation&quot; to THEIR way of believing. Which is the right one. So stop believing wrong.<br /> <br /> Sure, it seems a bit more ecumenical than the party line of the Catholic Church vs. the Orthodox Church vs. various other Churches (Coptic, Armenian, etc.) vs. various Heresies, etc., but it's not all THAT inclusive. Though, arguably, it might be slightly more or less inclusive, depending one whether they embrace non-Christians (Mithraists, Zoorastrians, Jews, etc.) within their ranks (which seems to be something that differs from place to place in the DA material.) <br /> <br /> And, even so, there is already organized dissent within the Fellowship... The groups that will eventually become the Chorus and the Cabal are already present. <br /> <br /> Where are the words from the gospels in all that? Well.... where are they in most of the different iterations of modern Christianity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T11:48:11-08:00","id":1022872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1022792#post1022792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. They believe in&quot;universal reconciliation&quot; to THEIR way of believing. Which is the right one. So stop believing wrong.<br /> <br /> Sure, it seems a bit more ecumenical than the party line of the Catholic Church vs. the Orthodox Church vs. various other Churches (Coptic, Armenian, etc.) vs. various Heresies, etc., but it's not all THAT inclusive. Though, arguably, it might be slightly more or less inclusive, depending one whether they embrace non-Christians (Mithraists, Zoorastrians, Jews, etc.) within their ranks (which seems to be something that differs from place to place in the DA material.)<br /> <br /> And, even so, there is already organized dissent within the Fellowship... The groups that will eventually become the Chorus and the Cabal are already present.<br /> <br /> Where are the words from the gospels in all that? Well.... where are they in most of the different iterations of modern Christianity?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> yeah but universal reconciliation implies that&quot;wrong&quot; has no ultimate penalty.<br /> unless they believe that the reconciliation will only happen so long as the &quot;good guys&quot; (them) win. but i don;t think it's mentioned anywhere","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T14:50:09-08:00","id":1022968,"title":"","content":"Humans have infinite capacities for hypocrisy. Remember, Christianity has claimed to be a religion of peace all throughout its history, but it was not until the last couple of centuries that some of its followers started to actually practice what they preached. Even Buddhism has experienced that type of hypocrisy, with the historical subjugation of the Bon religion in Tibet until the late 20th century.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T17:13:09-08:00","id":1023037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1022872#post1022872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> yeah but universal reconciliation implies that&quot;wrong&quot; has no ultimate penalty.<br /> unless they believe that the reconciliation will only happen so long as the &quot;good guys&quot; (them) win. but i don;t think it's mentioned anywhere</div> </div> </div> </div>Your core idea is not even vaguely born out in the Messianic Voices write up in DA. If they were as huggable as you seem to think they should be based on a very vague terminology added to a few quotes from a version of a translation of a document written down scores of years after they were supposedly spoken, they would not have the internal structure, internal conflicts, etc. they are described as having, front and center.<br /> <br /> A mission statement is not an iron clad definition of the totality of the source organization. In fact, it might have just as much relevance as a slogan in a commercial. Maybe &quot;universal reconciliation&quot; is just their version of &quot;Just do it&quot; or &quot;No fear&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T13:32:35-08:00","id":1023405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1022968#post1022968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans have infinite capacities for hypocrisy. Remember, Christianity has claimed to be a religion of peace all throughout its history, but it was not until the last couple of centuries that some of its followers started to actually practice what they preached. Even Buddhism has experienced that type of hypocrisy, with the historical subjugation of the Bon religion in Tibet until the late 20th century.</div> </div> </div> </div>From everything I've read, early Christians in the Roman Empire were very committed to ideals like pacifism, sharing wealth/property, caring for the needy, etc. To the point of being martyred for their beliefs. It's only some time after it became a state religion that the more aggressive practices started and maintaining power of the status quo became more important than following the moral precepts set forth in the New Testament.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:04:42-08:00","id":1023709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1023405#post1023405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From everything I've read, early Christians in the Roman Empire were very committed to ideals like pacifism, sharing wealth/property, caring for the needy, etc. To the point of being martyred for their beliefs. It's only some time after it became a state religion that the more aggressive practices started and maintaining power of the status quo became more important than following the moral precepts set forth in the New Testament.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> you are forgetting something important. up until 313 christians had no power. it's not they they were much better. it's that they were powerless.<br /> <br /> as early as the early second century ad they held that pagan gods were demons in disguise<br /> <br /> also to an extend persecution of christians was not quite what people imagine. not to say it didn't happen but it was usually much milder. for instance &quot;thrown at lions for being christians&quot; is a myth 100%","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T09:55:33-08:00","id":1023830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> also to an extend persecution of Christians was not quite what people imagine. not to say it didn't happen but it was usually much milder. for instance &quot;thrown at lions for being Christians&quot; is a myth 100% </div> </div> </div>Well not 100% but definitely not how popular movies define it. It wasn't always lions, and it wasn't just Christians, nor was it something that was common. Interestingly enough Christians are far more persecuted today than they ever were in the past. Especially in the Middle East.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T11:06:11-08:00","id":1023857,"title":"","content":"Okay, *this* is a good debate/topic-point, Mark. I am, for once, not contemplating how to beat you to death with a pillow...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense#post1022729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">at least in my opinion.<br /> from dark ages mage core rule book: these guys believe in universal reconciliation<br /> in lay terms this means that(eventually) everyone gets saved.</div> </div> </div> </div>While there is a good degree of truth to that statement/analysis, it's overly simplistic. &quot;Everyone getting saved&quot; doesn't mean that everyone will all be singing kumbaya together as their souls/essences &quot;reunite&quot; -- many aspects of The One will be reabsorbed as &quot;non-living/non-sentient&quot; aspects. That is, the reuniting of The One doesn't correlate with &quot;heaven&quot; to some of the more discordant shards; their rejoining will be a... process... a process that is the (P)urgatory that many are experiencing now both physically and spiritually/meta-physically. (That theoretically &quot;all will know the joy of being rejoined in The One&quot; is almost a secondary aspect to that... and one that perhaps sidesteps -- as religion is want to do -- the underlying metaphysical point that The One *desired* to be diverse in the first place... which complicates things on a level that is again easily overlooked....)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense#post1022729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but here is the issue. historically the justification for christian intolerance(and torture and executions etc) were the following two things.<br /> 1)jesus said&quot;love god and love others as yourself&quot;<br /> 2)jesus said &quot;i am the way and the truth no one comes to the father etc&quot; or &quot;whoever denies me i will also deny before the father&quot; or &quot;but he who does not believe is already lost for he has denied the son&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind, too, the oft-cited point that while it's easy to correlate the MV/later-CC with Christianity, that is a superficial perception that is as misleading as thinking all Ecstactics are hippie drug-addicts who all do things the same way and for a never-ending orgasm; or similarly that all Euthanatos are just shadowy murderers from a single far-eastern faith with no regard for the sanctity of life (which is very often not at all the case). While Christianity does gain influence in the MV/CC in the Dark-and-later (A)ges, there are a great many Voices who don't ascribe to that particular, specific manifestation of orthodoxy. Equally, it's easy for us, as readers/outside the game, to forget that a number of MVs wind up having spiritual awakenings (often, ironically, including their Awakenings, proper) that have them seeing the world/universe through the lens of their faith but in a manner that is nigh-to-actually heretical to the faith they ostensibly have. (That is, they can at times perceive &quot;God&quot;, et al, in a manner that is flat-out at odds with their more un(A)wakened brethren in the faith they share, both mundane mortal as well as numina-endowed faith-workers alike... if the MV isn't guarded about exactly how they phrase things, schisms of (F)aith can easily erupt... as they did in the centuries before-and-after the Dark Ages setting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> *****<br /> 1) Yes, Jesus said that. And plenty of Christians (even among the Awakened) ignored that left, right and center when it conflicted with their personal agendas. #ThatsOldNews<br /> 2) Yes, he said that to. Of course, the contextual meaning in that varied in applied interpretation among Gnostics and other early Christian groups in Real Life(tm), let alone in the WoD where things are much more up for grabs. (Many Gnostics, for example, ascribed the idea of &quot;the god-self&quot; which exists within all human beings as being the &quot;self&quot; through which (A)scension is found, and that the later applied Catholic and similar teachings/choice of wording-interpretations served more the desire to monopolize influence over the people/masses vs. proper spiritual awakening.) All of that goes again to show how it's very easy to over-simplify the perception of what, exactly, the MVs beliefs are (including how, despite the perceptions of other groups, there is more diversity among them than appears on the surface). It's often shocking to many outsiders to find (dependent, of course, on the time period in question) that some MVs of the past included worshipers of &quot;heathen&quot;/&quot;pagan&quot; (to some perspectives) deific manifestations, whether the old god(s) of Al'Khem, the Theoi of Greece/Rome (in their orthodox vs. later paganized identities, the latter reflected in The Old Faith and others), or other similar-such, including the at-times-subtle and other-times-overt differences that were &quot;in-house&quot; among the MV vis-a-vis Jews whose beliefs were old-school Kabbalah that very much conflicted with other MVs beliefs during the DA and later (earlier, sideways and in some contexts at all times). <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense#post1022729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">these are generally interpreted to mean that non christians(and heretics or at least serious ones) go to hell. even if said hell is a limbo/paradise of the unsaved&quot;<br /> so if we accept the above premises it makes perfect sense. to try and destroy other religions by any and all means. because you genuinely wish to save these people. even if a &quot;few&quot; have to be &quot;lost&quot; to make an example to the rest.<br /> even in versions of christianity(such as eastern orthodoxy i believe) where non christians can be saved this logic can still be applied to an extend. after all the new testament's morality is still the best way to avoid hell.<br /> <br /> but if premise number 2) is entirely wrong...then what is the point of all that violence?<br /> <br /> unless you are a gabrielite who believes premise number 2) is correct</div> </div> </div> </div>The underlying fundamentals of your questions/citations are predicated, themselves, on a narrow misperception about the MV/CC can be-and-are composed of, belief-wise, as I indicated further up. The Messianic &quot;intolerance&quot; is perfectly justifiable relative to the idea of discordant voices being brought into line with the harmony of The One; similarly, there are opposing &quot;songs&quot; and even &quot;silences&quot; (that is, the intruding forces of True Outsiders -- true (D)emons, those who are liken unto Jehovah but from outside his garden, etc.) that intrude on the music and lyrics of The One, in both small and large ways. Those, also, must be dealt with, with varying degrees of awareness and insight, than meets the casual eye....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T05:42:58-08:00","id":1024244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Just John, Forever...</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1023857#post1023857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, *this* is a good debate/topic-point, Mark. I am, for once, not contemplating how to beat you to death with a pillow...<br /> shall i consider my sins forgiven then?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> While there is a good degree of truth to that statement/analysis, it's overly simplistic. &quot;Everyone getting saved&quot; doesn't mean that everyone will all be singing kumbaya together as their souls/essences &quot;reunite&quot; -- many aspects of The One will be reabsorbed as &quot;non-living/non-sentient&quot; aspects. That is, the reuniting of The One doesn't correlate with &quot;heaven&quot; to some of the more discordant shards; their rejoining will be a... process... a process that is the (P)urgatory that many are experiencing now both physically and spiritually/meta-physically. (That theoretically &quot;all will know the joy of being rejoined in The One&quot; is almost a secondary aspect to that... and one that perhaps sidesteps -- as religion is want to do -- the underlying metaphysical point that The One *desired* to be diverse in the first place... which complicates things on a level that is again easily overlooked....)<br /> <br /> <br /> i see. so &quot;Everyone gets saved&quot; is more interpreted like &quot; when the one re-divides himself after the coming union ends everyone will still be present(so to speak) but while the actual period of union itsself may not be fire and brimstone this period of growth will still be &quot;direful&quot;(to use the eastern orthodox explanation of purgatory)<br /> if that so i kind of like it. it explain how the average messianic voice is intolerant( by today's standards) while still far better than your local friendly inquisitor AKA this guy<br /> <a href=\"http://berserk.wikia.com/wiki/Mozgus\" target=\"_blank\">http://berserk.wikia.com/wiki/Mozgus</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> Keep in mind, too, the oft-cited point that while it's easy to correlate the MV/later-CC with Christianity, that is a superficial perception that is as misleading as thinking all Ecstactics are hippie drug-addicts who all do things the same way and for a never-ending orgasm; or similarly that all Euthanatos are just shadowy murderers from a single far-eastern faith with no regard for the sanctity of life (which is very often not at all the case). While Christianity does gain influence in the MV/CC in the Dark-and-later (A)ges, there are a great many Voices who don't ascribe to that particular, specific manifestation of orthodoxy. Equally, it's easy for us, as readers/outside the game, to forget that a number of MVs wind up having spiritual awakenings (often, ironically, including their Awakenings, proper) that have them seeing the world/universe through the lens of their faith but in a manner that is nigh-to-actually heretical to the faith they ostensibly have. (That is, they can at times perceive &quot;God&quot;, et al, in a manner that is flat-out at odds with their more un(A)wakened brethren in the faith they share, both mundane mortal as well as numina-endowed faith-workers alike... if the MV isn't guarded about exactly how they phrase things, schisms of (F)aith can easily erupt... as they did in the centuries before-and-after the Dark Ages setting... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> IIRC this did happen in 1242(when the gabrielites are expelled precisely because they are extremists) and 1265 when the catholic church declares the messianics heretics.<br /> <br /> *****<br /> 1) Yes, Jesus said that. And plenty of Christians (even among the Awakened) ignored that left, right and center when it conflicted with their personal agendas. #ThatsOldNews<br /> 2) Yes, he said that to. Of course, the contextual meaning in that varied in applied interpretation among Gnostics and other early Christian groups in Real Life(tm), let alone in the WoD where things are much more up for grabs. (Many Gnostics, for example, ascribed the idea of &quot;the god-self&quot; which exists within all human beings as being the &quot;self&quot; through which (A)scension is found, and that the later applied Catholic and similar teachings/choice of wording-interpretations served more the desire to monopolize influence over the people/masses vs. proper spiritual awakening.) All of that goes again to show how it's very easy to over-simplify the perception of what, exactly, the MVs beliefs are (including how, despite the perceptions of other groups, there is more diversity among them than appears on the surface). It's often shocking to many outsiders to find (dependent, of course, on the time period in question) that some MVs of the past included worshipers of &quot;heathen&quot;/&quot;pagan&quot; (to some perspectives) deific manifestations, whether the old god(s) of Al'Khem, the Theoi of Greece/Rome (in their orthodox vs. later paganized identities, the latter reflected in The Old Faith and others), or other similar-such, including the at-times-subtle and other-times-overt differences that were &quot;in-house&quot; among the MV vis-a-vis Jews whose beliefs were old-school Kabbalah that very much conflicted with other MVs beliefs during the DA and later (earlier, sideways and in some contexts at all times).<br /> <br /> by &quot;orthodox later paganised identities&quot; are you referring to greco-roman neoplatonism? if so then neoplatonism came later not first. unless im misunderstanding something?<br /> <br /> <br /> [COLOR=#252C2F][FONT=Helvetica][SIZE=13px]<br /> The underlying fundamentals of your questions/citations are predicated, themselves, on a narrow misperception about the MV/CC can be-and-are composed of, belief-wise, as I indicated further up. The Messianic &quot;intolerance&quot; is perfectly justifiable relative to the idea of discordant voices being brought into line with the harmony of The One; similarly, there are opposing &quot;songs&quot; and even &quot;silences&quot; (that is, the intruding forces of True Outsiders -- true (D)emons, those who are liken unto Jehovah but from outside his garden, etc.) that intrude on the music and lyrics of The One, in both small and large ways. Those, also, must be dealt with, with varying degrees of awareness and insight, than meets the casual eye....</div> </div> </div> </div>it propably doesn't help that orthodox messianic voices see jehovah/the demiurge/yaldabaoth/ as the One . hell it's implied that even most abyss demons make this confusion which has some interesting implications i think<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> damn it for some reason my words are part of the greyed out area. is there some button i forgot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T18:08:03-08:00","id":1025654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1023830#post1023830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well not 100% but definitely not how popular movies define it. It wasn't always lions, and it wasn't just Christians, nor was it something that was common. Interestingly enough Christians are far more persecuted today than they ever were in the past. Especially in the Middle East.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not technically true. While the Christians in Western Asia are being oppressed because of the overthrow of Saddam Hussein and the civil war in Syria, Christians are the dominant religion in Australia, Europe, North America, and South America. It is also the fastest growing religion in Africa and India, despite religious discrimination and persecution. Evangelical Christianity is the fastest growing religion in the world and has been for fifty years, growing at three times the rate of population growth, and more children are born to Christian households than Islamic households. In many ways, it is the Golden Age of Christianity as, despite growing secularism across the developed world, it is growing throughout the developing world. In addition, Christian nations control 60% of the wealth of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-02T22:26:33-08:00","id":1025740,"title":"","content":"They're hypocrites. It's a thing that human beings tend to be a lot, so don't be surprised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1675-weirdboyz","name":"Weirdboyz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1675_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T10:28:57-08:00","id":1026022,"title":"","content":"Over 300 Christians are martyred (murdered) monthly for their faith. More than 700 are violently persecuted. <br /> <br /> Granted the number of those persecuted are higher today than in antiquity simply due to population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:05:24-08:00","id":1033421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1026022#post1026022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over 300 Christians are martyred (murdered) monthly for their faith. More than 700 are violently persecuted.<br /> <br /> Granted the number of those persecuted are higher today than in antiquity simply due to population.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> to make a long story short, with a few exceptions(e.g diocletian,galerius etc) christianity was not &quot;exactly&quot; illegal in the roman empire. essentially the emperors established a system of don't ask don't tell. not for christian beliefs(they weren't illegal) but for christians not joining the imperial cult etc. so magistrates were not supposed to actively search for violators. in case private citizens made an accusation then the burden of proof lay on them with very strict penalties if proven to be liars<br /> <br /> as i see it it was propably feared that not doing your part for the state sacrifices(aside from offending the gods) would disrupt society. in the same way that people like rousseau disapproved of atheism for that reason. fun fact: atheism was originally defined as: being against the gods of your country","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-17T10:28:37-08:00","id":1033445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1033421#post1033421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> to make a long story short, with a few exceptions(e.g diocletian,galerius etc) christianity was not &quot;exactly&quot; illegal in the roman empire. essentially the emperors established a system of don't ask don't tell. not for christian beliefs(they weren't illegal) but for christians not joining the imperial cult etc. so magistrates were not supposed to actively search for violators. in case private citizens made an accusation then the burden of proof lay on them with very strict penalties if proven to be liars</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This describes the treatment of early Christians during the reign of Hadrian or perhaps Trajan. Christian persecution in the Roman Empire was varied. A lot of it depended on politics and the personal beliefs of the governing elite. Some emperors were quite harsh, though perhaps not to the degree that the historian Eusebius claimed. Nero was pretty vicious, and anti-Jewish violence in Ancient Rome would indiscriminately fall on early Christians too. Valerian had some nasty edicts concerning Christians also, condemning church leadership to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T02:56:43-08:00","id":1034494,"title":"","content":"still 2 periods of big discrimination ( 250-260 303-311) (nero doesn't count as his purge was only limited to rome. plus by the end of his reign he was insane) versus a discrimination starting from 325 or 341 and going on until the french revolution when it was <b>forcibly </b>stopped(the church didn't officially change its views until 1965 i think) doesn't really speak well for the religion of &quot;love&quot; if you ask me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T05:33:16-08:00","id":1034530,"title":"","content":"Christanity isn't a religion of love. It's a relationship of forgiveness. Whether or not those who claim to belong to it act it out or not is another matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-19T12:11:29-08:00","id":1034766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1022729-messianic-voices-intolerance-makes-no-sense?p=1034530#post1034530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Christanity isn't a religion of love. It's a relationship of forgiveness.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can be both of those things. Religions aren't limited to just one, overarching virtue or theme. Not unless it's a fictional religion, invented by writers who only put a surface level amount of thought into what it's about. Indeed, much of the depth of Mage Traditions comes from when players dig deeper than the archetypes of their characters, and research what their particular culture or philosophy believes.<br /> <br /> But yes, it's unfortunate that so many people identify as Christians and believe in Christ, yet don't understand or practice his teachings (if not to the letter, than at least in spirit and intent). It's disheartening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}